@startuml
title Actual Python module dependencies — separate normal and artillery paths
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

component "app.py" as App
component "src.fow_combat.view" as NormalView
component "src.fow_combat.controller" as NormalController
component "src.fow_combat.model" as NormalModel
component "src.fow_combat.artillery_view" as ArtilleryView
component "src.fow_combat.artillery_controller" as ArtilleryController
component "src.fow_combat.artillery" as ArtilleryDomain
package "src.fow_combat.domain (direct shooting data types)" {
  component "domain.inputs" as Inputs
  component "domain.to_hit" as ToHit
  component "domain.firepower" as Firepower
}
component "Streamlit" as Streamlit
component "NumPy" as NumPy

App --> NormalView : imports Normal widgets/rendering
App --> NormalController : calculate(CombatInput)
App --> ArtilleryView : selected Artillery route
NormalView --> NormalController : CombatInput / display result
NormalController --> NormalModel : simulate
NormalModel --> NumPy : binomial draws / arrays
NormalView --> NumPy : histogram / summary statistics
ArtilleryView --> ArtilleryController : ArtilleryCommand
ArtilleryView --> ArtilleryDomain : command and result types
ArtilleryView --> ArtilleryDomain : rules registry options
ArtilleryController --> ArtilleryDomain : calculate_artillery
ArtilleryDomain --> ArtilleryDomain : exact state DP / policy lookup
Inputs --> ToHit
Inputs --> Firepower
NormalView --> Streamlit
ArtilleryView --> Streamlit
App --> Streamlit

note bottom of ArtilleryDomain
Exact probability propagation is pure Python.
It uses no NumPy, RNG, or direct-shooting domain input types.
end note

note bottom of Inputs
Direct-shooting data contracts remain separate from
both implemented UI calculation routes.
end note
@enduml
